course: dictionary
lesson: 13267
title: Goggles: protection or a joke?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Goggles can mean two things, so the words around it tell you which one is meant. Goggles are special glasses that fit tightly round your eyes to protect them from water, wind, snow, dust, chemicals or flying bits. «Sam put on his safety goggles before he mixed the liquids in science.» The clues are science and mixing liquids, so the goggles protect his eyes.
explain: «Lily swam a length underwater, and her swimming goggles kept the pool water out of her eyes.» Here the clue is swimming and water. Goggles can also be a jokey word for glasses. «Grandad squinted at the menu. "Pass me my goggles, I can't read a word!"» The joke tells you he means ordinary glasses.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Does «Sam put on his glasses that protect his eyes before he mixed the liquids» still make sense? Yes, so you have understood it. Goggles is also a plural word, so we say «a pair of goggles».
fact: Goggles are special glasses that fit tightly round your eyes to protect them.
fact: «Safety goggles» protect eyes from chemicals, sparks and flying bits, so always wear them when your teacher tells you to.
fact: «Swimming goggles» keep water out of your eyes so you can see under water.
fact: «Ski goggles» protect your eyes from glare and wind on the snow.
fact: Goggles is a plural word, so say «a pair of goggles», and you can also use it as a jokey word for glasses.
exercise: «In science, Priya wore safety goggles to keep chemicals out of her eyes.» What did the goggles protect? | Her shoes | Her hair | *Her eyes | Her ears
exercise: Grandad says, «Pass me my goggles, I can't read the small print.» What does goggles mean here? | Swimming goggles that keep water out | *Glasses, a jokey word for ordinary glasses | Chemicals that burn | Skiing goggles against snow
exercise: «Ravi pulled his goggles down before he skied down the hill.» Why did Ravi wear goggles? | To hear better | To keep his hair dry | To keep his hat on | *To protect his eyes from glare and wind
test: «Always put on your goggles before you mix the chemicals.» What does goggles mean here? | A kind of swimming costume | Jokey glasses for a laugh | Glasses for reading | *Special glasses that protect the eyes
test: Which phrase is correct for one set of goggles? | a goggly | a goggle | a goggles | *a pair of goggles
exam: Which sentence uses goggles as a jokey word for ordinary glasses? | Ski goggles protect your eyes from glare | *Grandad squinted at the menu through his goggles and laughed | Safety goggles stop chemicals splashing | Swimming goggles keep water out of your eyes
